15 August 2006)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Pan American Health Organization</collab></person-group><source>Health of the Americas</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>PAHO</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.paho.org/english/HIA1998/Peru.pdf"/><comment>(accessed 15 August 2006)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bust&#x000ed;os</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><source>La Salud P&#x000fa;blica Durante la Rep&#x000fa;blica Olig&#x000e1;rquica Segunda parte 1896&#x02013;1933 (Primera versi&#x000f3;n)</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Lima: Oficina General de Investigaciones UNMSM</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Peruvian College of Physicians</collab></person-group><source>Official statistics</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Statistic Records Office. Lima</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nigenda</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Machado</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Castrillon</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Arroya</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Soderlund N, Mendoza-Arana P, Goudge J</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The impact of health care reform on the professional regulation of physicians in Latin America</article-title><source>The New Public/Private Mix in Health: Exploring the Changing Landscape</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Geneva: Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research</publisher-name><fpage>13</fpage><lpage>34</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mendoza-Arana</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Soderlund N, Mendoza-Arana P, Goudge J</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Potential of private practitioners to deliver public health services in Peru</article-title><source>The New Public/Private Mix in Health: Exploring the Changing Landscape</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Geneva: Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research</publisher-name><fpage>60</fpage><lpage>72</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jumpa</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mills</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Dual Practice of Public Sector Health Care Providers in Peru</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Report to the Health Economics and Financing Programme, London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bust&#x000ed;os</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><source>Per&#x000fa; La Salud P&#x000fa;blica Durante la Rep&#x000fa;blica Demoliberal Primera parte 1933 &#x02013; 1968 (Primera versi&#x000f3;n)</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Lima: Consejo Superior de Investigaciones UNMSM</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Government of Peru</collab></person-group><source>Decreto Legislativo 559 Ley del Trabajo M&#x000e9;dico</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>Lima</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Government of Peru</collab></person-group><source>Ley General de Salud</source><year>1997</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.gerenciasalud.com/leygeneraldesaludperu.htm"/><comment>(accessed 5 July 2006)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Webb</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Valencia</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>Human Resources in Public Health and Education in Peru</source><year>2005</year><volume>1</volume><publisher-name>RECURSO Peru Project, Policy Recommendations and Summary. World Bank</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www1.worldbank.org/publicsector/Webb%20Valencia%20Sept%2005.doc"/><comment>(accessed 15 August 2006)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>United States Department of State</collab></person-group><source>Background Note: Peru</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.state.gov/r/pa/ei/bgn/35762.htm#econ"/><comment>(accessed 9 February 2007)</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muraleedharan</surname><given-names>VR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ram Prasad</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The trade in human organs in Tamil Nadu: the anatomy of regulatory failure</article-title><source>Health Economics, Policy and Law</source><year>2006</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>17</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>